From 5858d89286dd16aa840d32ac449c0f5454bd9788 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 15:32:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(post): refuse a G83 dwell on the grblHAL and Tormach
 posts

The LinuxCNC G-code reference, Tormach's PathPilot G83 page and the
grblHAL core code list give G83 no P word. The two posts dropped a
deep-peck dwell with no message. They now refuse it by name before any
G83 block is written, with the message text of the Fanuc-family
refusal (#1820). A G83 with no dwell posts as before.

Pinned by crates/post/tests/g83_dwell_linuxcnc.rs.

Fixes #2348

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
